  "notes": "Means to endure, put up with, or hold back. Covers physical pain, emotional frustration, and self-restraint (e.g., resisting temptation). Highly valued in Japanese culture as a personal virtue.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n- No standard intransitive pair\n- Pattern: [noun]⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{我慢|がまん}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {我慢|がまん}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to endure, be patient\n- {我慢|がまん}⟦できる→できる：00557_dekiru⟧/⟦できない→できる：00557_dekiru⟧: can/cannot stand it\n- ⟦{我慢強|がまんづよ}い→我慢強い：07164_gamanzuyoi⟧: patient, persevering (adjective)\n- {我慢|がまん}⟦の→の：09472_no⟧⟦{限界|げんかい}→限界：02715_genkai⟧: the limit of one's patience\n\nUSAGE:\nOften used when someone is bearing discomfort or holding back desires. Children are frequently told to {我慢|がまん}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧ — it is considered an important life skill.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{忍耐|にんたい}→忍耐：05212_nintai⟧: patience, endurance (more formal/literary)\n- ⟦{辛抱|しんぼう}→辛抱：05101_shinbou⟧: perseverance (emphasizes long-term endurance)\n- ⟦{堪|こら}える→堪える：08995_koraeru⟧: to bear, withstand (verb)",
